From 79e68af289ae7ccba094e569857f018f65041fd3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jakob Linke <jgruber@chromium.org>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 10:41:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] regexp: Handle supplementary case equivalents with ICU 79

Upstream: https://github.com/v8/v8/commit/f607706154eabc4a949628a88b38dbe95cd2274c

Unicode 18 adds U+1DF95 to the case-equivalence class of U+00DF and
U+1E9E. Filter supplementary characters from non-Unicode closures and
desugar the affected BMP literals in Unicode mode.

Adapt the upstream fix to V8 14.6's RegExpCaseFolding and existing
closure call sites. Keep SpecialAddSet and the UTF-16 assertion. Run
the upstream JavaScript cases in Node's parallel suite. Backreferences
with differing UTF-16 widths remain tracked in crbug.com/571793821.

Bug: https://crbug.com/571232615
Bug: https://crbug.com/571668686
---
